---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: "How do I split a PDF into single pages?", a: "Open Split PDF, choose Every page and click Split. You get one PDF per page, downloaded together as a .zip file." },
  { q: "Can I split a PDF into chapters?", a: "Yes. Choose By ranges and type the page ranges, for example 1-12, 13-30, 31-48. Each range becomes its own PDF." },
  { q: "Does splitting reduce quality?", a: "No. Pages are copied exactly as they are, so text stays selectable and images keep their resolution." },
];
---
<GuideLayout slug="split-pdf-into-separate-files" faqs={faqs}>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> open <a href="/split-pdf">Split PDF</a>, select your file and pick how to split it: <strong>Every page</strong> (one file per page), <strong>By ranges</strong> (for example <code>1-3, 8-10</code>) or <strong>Select pages</strong> (tap the pages you want). Click Split and download. The PDF never leaves your device.</p>

  <h2>Three ways to split</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Every page:</strong> best for scanned bundles where each page is a separate document, like a stack of receipts or certificates. You get a .zip with <code>file-1.pdf</code>, <code>file-2.pdf</code> and so on.</li>
    <li><strong>By ranges:</strong> best for chapters or sections. Type ranges separated by commas. Each range becomes its own PDF, or tick the option to combine them into one file.</li>
    <li><strong>Select pages:</strong> best on a phone. Tap the thumbnails of the pages you want and save them as one new PDF. This is the same as <a href="/extract-pdf-pages">Extract Pages</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step by step</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <a href="/split-pdf">pdfsherpa.com/split-pdf</a> on your phone or computer.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Select PDF</strong> and choose the file. Page thumbnails appear.</li>
    <li>Pick a split method and enter ranges or tap pages.</li>
    <li>Click the split button. Several files download as one .zip, a single file downloads directly.</li>
  </ol>

  <AdSlot variant="inline" slot="guide-article" />

  <h2>Common examples</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Job applications:</strong> a portal wants your degree and your experience letter as separate uploads, but you scanned them together. Split by ranges.</li>
    <li><strong>Bank statements:</strong> send only the months someone asked for with Select pages.</li>
    <li><strong>Books and notes:</strong> break a 300-page PDF into chapters so it opens faster on a phone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the page numbers on the thumbnails, not the numbers printed on the pages. A cover page often makes them differ by one or two.</li>
    <li>On a phone, the .zip opens in the Files app (iPhone) or Files by Google (Android). Tap it to unzip.</li>
    <li>Need to remove only a few pages and keep the rest together? <a href="/delete-pdf-pages">Delete Pages</a> is quicker.</li>
    <li>If each new file must be under a size limit, run it through <a href="/compress-pdf">Compress PDF</a> afterwards.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Private by design</h2>
  <p>Splitting happens in your browser with the open-source pdf-lib library. Your document is not uploaded, so it is safe for contracts, statements and ID scans.</p>
</GuideLayout>
